<title>FRANCE: Uganda sees 1996/97 coffee output at 3.4 mln bags.</title>
<headline>Uganda sees 1996/97 coffee output at 3.4 mln bags.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uganda expects to produce 3.4 million 60-kg bags of coffee in the 1996/1997 fiscal year, Ugandan Planning and Economic Development Minister Richard Kaijuka said on Friday.</p>
<p>Kaijuka, in Paris for talks with the World Bank, read the figures at a news conference.</p>
<p>On November 12, the state-owned Uganda Coffee Development Authority (UCDA) said coffee procurement in the October/September 1996/97 year would be between 3.6 and 3.8 million bags, down from 4.2 million in the previous year.</p>
<p>At the time, the UCDA blamed the drop on the cyclical nature of perennial crops, hailstorms in August and September and coffee wilt disease in some districts.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5071</p>
</text>
